> >
> > I think I understand but I am running into some issues. I am starting by testing a function version of the sampler. When I try to compile I get the error message
> >
> > Error in matchKeywordCodeMemberFun(code, nfProc) :
> >   Cannot handle this expression (looks like a model with an invalid member function call?): model$getDependencies(nnames[numnodes])
> >
> > I know you said to put this in the setup part of the function but in my case I have a multivariate sampler. Not all univariate nodes assigned to the sampler get updated each iteration. Therefore, to be efficient I am only running calculate on the univariate nodes that get updated. So, I think I need a list of dependencies i.e. depend_list[[node]]= model$getDependencies(node) where node is in expandNodeNames(target). But, I am not sure how to do this. Any suggestions?
> >
> > On Thursday, May 28, 2020 at 1:58:16 PM UTC-4, pdevalpine wrote:
> > > Hi Dirk,
> > >
> > > The rules for a sampler are that it can expect upon entry to have the model in a fully calculated state (so, for example, model$getLogProb(nodes) can be used reliably, since this pulls cached values of log probs without calculating them) and to have the mvSaved and the model be fully in sync (all values matching).  That means that for a sampler to work correctly in the system (assuming it might be used amid other samplers in the MCMC configuration), it must ensure those two conditions are met again before it exits, for the benefit of the next sampler.
> > >
> > > Specifically, if you have a sampler that changes the value of model[[target]], it is the sampler's responsibility to ensure those conditions upon exit.  The typical way to do so is
> > > In setup code:
