Can you give a minimal fully reproducible example?

Here is what I notice:

If target is multiple nodes (or even if it is a single node), you might want
prev <- values(model, target)
and you can later use
values(model, target) <- proposed
for example.

If target is a single node, then
model[[target]] should behave with the dimension of the node.  For example if it is a matrix, then model[[target]][i, j] should work.
but in that case, in setup, you might want returnScalarComponents=TRUE in expandNodeNames in order to determine the length.

Oh, I think I see more of what is happening.  "S[dq]" will not work.  The variable dq will not be evaluated as part of a node name, and even if it did, a logical subset will not work that way.

Does
model$getNodeNames("S", dataOnly = TRUE)
give what you want?

-Perry

