Hi Perry,

"S" is a vector node, so like "S[1]", "S[2]",...,"S[T+1]". Some of S is data and I only want to sample the non data nodes which is why I used "S[dq]" as target. I have found a workaround for now. I can calculate the time index ct for the node easily. So I am just replacing the problematic code with

prev <- model$S[ct]
instead of prev <- model[[target]][zt]

where ct is the time index of the node (zt is the index of sampled nodes only). Then in the setup I only use the target which is equal to "S[dq]". This seems to work so far but ill let you know if I run into any issues.

